					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#438">KoFbank</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							Our guild now has a bank mule. Xarulle, our banker, has created the character Kofbank to be our bank. KoF stands for keepers of Fire bank stands for bank. The bank rules are the following<br />
<br />
1: Donations are accepted, not required<br />
<br />
2: Items can be withdrawn for use by Main Character only, no alts. <br />
<br />
3: Items attained during guild raid are guild items (stated previously) when you no longer need they are turned over to the bank so someone else can get them.<br />
<br />
4: There is no selling of items attained during a raid. <br />
<br />
5: If an item is in the bank for a long period of time with no claims on it then it can be sold by the banker to become guild funds. <br />
<br />
6: The guild funds obtained by the sale of such items will be used to further the trade skills of tailors, blacksmiths, jewlers, and fletchers that are in the guild, and to buy better items that can be put into the guild bank.<br />
<br />
i hope everyone enjoys the use of the bank and if you find an item that can be put to use in the guild please donate it to the bank so that it can be circulated (good example would be monster drop spells) <br />
<br />
Thank You
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							<br>
														<strong>By:</strong>
							<span class="name"> <a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2836">Olthar Othlinden</a> at 11:03 AM PDT - April 21st, 2002</span>
						</td>
					</tr>
